#################################################################
# VSON v1 conformance test suite — the manifest.
#
# docs/vson.md §2.2 is the normative half of this file: an implementation
# claims VSON v1 conformance by passing this suite, and the suite is what
# "passing" means. Through v1.3.0 the specification defined a conformant
# consumer as one that "accepts every document accepted by the Python
# references plus pyshacl" — a definition no second implementation can be
# checked against without running the first, and one that makes every
# accident of the reference implementations normative. This manifest replaces
# it with a list of documents and the verdict each one MUST get.
#
# Modelled on the W3C SHACL test suite: mf: for the manifest structure, sht:
# for the data/shapes pair of a validation action, sh: for the pinned
# validation report, and five VSON-local test types in the vsont: namespace
# for the things SHACL's suite has no vocabulary for — the two hand-written
# surfaces, the denotation relation of §4.6, and the exporters.
#
#   vsont:ParsePTest       VSON-P (Appendix B) source -> accepted or rejected
#   vsont:ParseXTest       VSON-X (Appendix D) source -> accepted, or rejected
#                          at a named §D.7 row
#   vsont:ValidationTest   a document -> the three gates of §2.1, with the
#                          report pinned to sh:sourceShape / sh:focusNode /
#                          sh:resultPath / sh:resultSeverity
#   vsont:EquivalenceTest  one or more documents -> the RDFC-1.0 canonical
#                          hash of §4.6 they all MUST have
#   vsont:ExportTest       a document + an exporter -> byte-frozen output
#
# The vocabulary is declared in vocabulary.ttl beside this file, and
# tools/conformance_runner.py refuses to run a manifest that uses a term the
# vocabulary does not declare — the same closure C2 asks of a document.
#
# WHAT IS PINNED, AND WHY THAT SHAPE
#
# A validation result names its *named* source shape. VSON-S states its
# cardinality and value-space constraints as sh:property blank nodes nested
# inside named node shapes, and a blank node cannot be pinned across runs, so
# the runner resolves each result to the nearest named ancestor
# (tools/validate_report.py named_shape) and this file pins that. Where the
# focus node is itself a blank node — a Quality or a SpatialFact the VSON-X
# emitter synthesised — vsont:focusNodeKind vsont:BlankNode is pinned instead
# of an identity that changes on every parse.
#
# Expected results are exhaustive. A document pinned with one sh:result MUST
# produce exactly one, which is what makes an over-firing shape a red build
# rather than an unnoticed one.
#
# HOW THIS FILE IS MAINTAINED
#
# By hand. There is no --freeze: unlike tests/fixtures/canonical/hashes.txt,
# nothing here is regenerated from a run, because the point of a pinned
# expectation is that a human decided it. Every entry was authored against
# the shape or the clause it exercises and then checked against a reference
# run; a run that disagrees is a question to answer, not a fixture to rewrite.
#
# COVERAGE
#
# vsont:clause, vsont:section, vsont:shape and vsont:enum on each entry are
# what docs/vson.md §2.2's coverage table is generated from
# (`python3 -m tools.conformance_runner --coverage-table`); the runner
# compares that table against the copy §2.2 publishes on every run and fails
# the build when the two disagree, so the specification cannot claim coverage
# this manifest lacks. The exemption block at the foot of this file is the
# honest half: a shape no input can trip is recorded there with the property
# of the shape that makes it so, and a shape that is merely untested is not —
# the runner rejects a shapes file carrying a named shape that is neither
# exercised nor exempted.
#################################################################

@prefix mf:    <http://www.w3.org/2001/sw/DataAccess/tests/test-manifest#> .
@prefix sht:   <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl-test#> .
@prefix sh:    <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix rdfs:  <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:   <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix owl:   <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix dc:    <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix vso:   <https://w3id.org/vson/v1/ontology#> .
@prefix vss:   <https://w3id.org/vson/v1/shapes#> .
@prefix rcc:   <https://w3id.org/vson/v1/rcc8#> .
@prefix vsont: <https://w3id.org/vson/v1/conformance#> .
@prefix t:     <https://w3id.org/vson/v1/conformance/tests#> .


<https://w3id.org/vson/v1/conformance/manifest>
